.TH RPE 1 "2026-07-09" "reta arch mojo" "Reta commands"
.SH NAME
rpe \- run one Reta prompt command with Emacs-style output formatting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rpe
.RI command ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rpe
is a one-shot Reta prompt profile for Emacs-oriented output.  It executes a
single prompt command and exits.  For non-
.B reta
prompt commands it wraps the command so that Emacs output is selected and
headings are suppressed.  For direct
.B reta
commands it appends the corresponding
.B -ausgabe --art=emacs --keineueberschriften
output options.
.PP
Historically, the fallback argument profile for
.B rpe
is equivalent to
.B -vi -e -befehl
plus the Emacs-output transformation.
.SH COMMANDS
.B rpe
accepts the same one-shot prompt command language as
.BR rpb (1),
including
.BR prim ,
.BR multis ,
.BR modulo ,
.BR abc ,
short table commands and full
.B reta
commands.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/rpe
Default public executable for a standard installation.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/reta/libreta_prompt_interactive_mojo.so
Interactive/profile boundary used by
.BR rpe .
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/reta/libreta_prompt_mojo.so
Shared prompt execution library.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
rpe prim 60
rpe reta -h
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rp (1),
.BR rpl (1),
.BR rpb (1),
.BR reta (1)
